From bfe2014084a62bc9c15358ee45c3fbcc16700f91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][dvbridge] A part of a picture copied into textures of
 its own size

The bridge draws a picture from textures of the picture's own size and
nothing else (dvbridge_gl_frame_import()): every pass that reads at an
edge replicates the edge of the picture there. A 3D picture holds two
views, side by side or one above the other (MV-HEVC and MVC as Kodi puts
their views side by side, a side-by-side or top-and-bottom file). Drawn
as a crop of that picture, a view reads the other view's samples across
the seam (measured on the software renderer: 3 of the 960 columns of a
1080p view in half side by side differ from the same picture in 2D), and
a picture of two 3840x2160 views is wider than the 4096 samples the
bridge takes in.

dvbridge_gl_part_copy() copies one part of a picture's planes, in the
layouts the bridge imports, into textures of the part's own size, kept
from one picture to the next and made again where the size or the layout
changes. The copy is glCopyImageSubData() (OpenGL ES 3.2, or
GL_EXT_copy_image / GL_OES_copy_image): the samples as they are, of any
format, without a pass of its own. A part of half a chroma sample, or one
past the picture, is refused. Drawn from such a part, a view is the same
picture as in 2D, value for value (tools/regress/dvbridge, stage
stereo3d).

Nothing calls it yet: the window system takes it for 3D pictures in the
next change.
